[[File:Bloody Tree (Beta 48.1).png|thumb|228x228px|Beta 48.1]]
Bloody Tree was added in '''Beta 30.0'''. Originally, it was a 2G 2/1 monster that, with Magic, could trigger the Dust effect of an ally monster at will (though not affecting it, effectively triggering a copy of the effect in a similar matter as Pre-Beta 46.0 [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Goner_Kid Goner Kid]), but only if that monster's cost is 3G or lower.
[[File:Bloody Tree (Beta 49.1).png|thumb|228x228px|Beta 49.1]]
'''Beta 48.1''' completely changed it, most likely due to the changes made to the [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Angel_of_Death Lost Souls] around that time. It's now a 6G 5/6 monster with the Magic effect of dealing Fatigue DMG to the opponent (DMG taken for failing to draw a card due to an empty deck or use of [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Artifacts#Preservation Preservation]). This is an almost identical recreation of Pre-Beta 38.2 [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Shambling_Mass Shambling Mass]. '''Beta 49.1''' reduced its HP to 4, while '''Beta 52.0''' increased its ATK to 6.

=== Stats ===
ATK:
